# Problem overview

For the Vision function of LobeChat, the image Base64 data requested may be compressed, resulting in the inability to call the Gemini Pro Vision model through the Google Vertex AI API.

# Description of the reproduction process

Open LobeChat and configure APIKey and APIEndpoint

The LobeChat front-end selects the `gpt-4-vision-preview` model. After the transfer back-end receives the program request, it rewrites this model to `gemini-pro-vision` and then converts the request body into one that complies with the Google Cloud Vertex AI standard. When the request body is sent to the Google Cloud Vertex AI API, a 400 error message will be received, prompting "Provided image is not valid.".

