Website address that provides GPT4v compatible API: `https://www.ohmygpt.com`

At the `https://api.ohmygpt.com/v1/chat/completions` API endpoint, a `gemini-pro-vision` multi-modal model inference service compatible with the `gpt-4-vision-preview` standard is provided,` Just specify `gemini-pro-vision` for the model` parameter.

## problem analysis

LobeChat may have compressed the image, causing the Google Cloud API to not accept it.

LobeChat can normally request Google's gemini-pro-vision because LobeChat may be connected to `https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com` instead of the connected Google Cloud Vertex AI API. Gemini Pro Vision related interfaces cannot accept sending from LobeChat. Come over the image Base64 data.

## suggestion

- (If the image is compressed/processed) Do not compress/process the user's pasted image by default. This may not be an expected behavior. You may consider adding a configurable item in the settings.
- `Settings`=>`Language Model`=>`OpenAI Settings` section, add a `Custom Vision Model Names` optional configuration item, indicating that these are compatible with OpenAI's `gpt-4-vision-preview` standard API Multi-modal models can upload images to facilitate users to call the multi-modal model API similar to the above compatibility.


