> Hello, @Xeelix! I'm here to help you with any bugs, questions, or contributions you have. Let's see if we can solve this together.
> 
> Yes, there is a way to disable "Manage files and knowledge base" and just temporarily upload photos when communicating with the vision model when `NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVICE_MODE=server` is enabled.
> 
> In the provided code, the `canUploadImage` variable determines whether the image upload functionality is enabled based on the current model. You can control the upload options by modifying the `items` array in the `FileUpload` component.
> 
> To disable the "Manage files and knowledge base" and only allow temporary photo uploads, you can adjust the `items` array to only include the image upload option and ensure that other upload options are disabled or removed.
> 
> Here is the modified code:
> 
> ```tsx
> const items: MenuProps['items'] = [
>   {
>     disabled: !canUploadImage,
>     icon: <Icon icon={ImageUp} style={{ fontSize: '16px' }} />,
>     key: 'upload-image',
>     label: canUploadImage ? (
>       <Upload
>         accept={'image/*'}
>         beforeUpload={async (file) => {
>           await upload([file]);
> 
>           return false;
>         }}
>         multiple
>         showUploadList={false}
>       >
>         <div className={cx(hotArea)}>{t('upload.action.imageUpload')}</div>
>       </Upload>
>     ) : (
>       <Tooltip placement={'right'} title={t('upload.action.imageDisabled')}>
>         <div className={cx(hotArea)}>{t('upload.action.imageUpload')}</div>
>       </Tooltip>
>     ),
>   },
> ];
> ```
> 
> Additionally, to ensure that the "Manage files and knowledge base" feature is disabled when in server mode, you can modify the `Upload` component to check the `enableKnowledgeBase` flag from the server configuration and render the appropriate mode:
